<title>FRANCE: Strauss-Kahn sees room for lower rates after euro.</title>
<headline>Strauss-Kahn sees room for lower rates after euro.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Dominique Strauss-Kahn said on Tuesday that the launch of the euro should open the way for lower interest rates.</p>
<p>&quot;The euro will allow lower rates...through a better management of prices and a better management of budget stability, to have lower interest rates, which favour growth,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;The room for lower interest rates is after the launch of the euro,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>This was the reason to launch the single currency.</p>
</text>
